# ServiceNow repo discovery

Applies to ServiceNow scoped application exports in Git (`**/update/**/*.xml`, etc.).

**`author_elective_update/`:** ignore for discovery and navigation unless the task is finding a **deleted record** or **application configuration stored only there**. See **`servicenow-xml-git-exports.mdc`**.

For **code review** priorities and JavaScript language level, see **`servicenow-xml-review.mdc`**.

## Registry MCP

Use **servicenow-xml-registry** before a workspace-wide search:

| Tool | Use for |
|------|---------|
| **`search_records`** | Find export rows by substring / table |
| **`lookup_by_name`** | Exact display name / `api_name` / declaration name |
| **`lookup_script_include`** | Script Include / UI Script (bundled + workspace) |
| **`get_workspace_app`** | Scope, `jsLevel` (`ES5` or `ES12`), `supportsES12`, and `restrictTableAccess` |
| **`registry_diagnostics_context`** | Symbol counts plus the app snapshot |
| **`list_tables` / `get_table` / `list_columns` / `search_schema`** | One dictionary: platform pack plus project `sys_dictionary` / `<database>` exports. Project columns win. Each field has `source`: `platform` or `project` |
| **`references_to` / `references_from`** | sys_id edges for one record. `targetState` is `in_project`, `deleted`, or `not_in_project` |
| **`list_reference_issues`** | Deleted-target references (same errors as the editor). Pass `includeNotInProject: true` to also list ids that are not in the export; those are not Problems-panel diagnostics |
| **`lookup_scripting_name`** | Platform API docs attached to Registry symbols |
| **`get_js_performance_meta` / `search_js_performance` / `lookup_js_performance`** | Bundled JavaScript performance evidence |

Workspace rows come from `.servicenow-xml/registry-cache.json`, written when the extension scans the folder. Do not read or regenerate `index.json`.

## Other custom MCPs

| Server | Use for |
|--------|---------|
| **servicenow-xml-instance** | Live read-only `list_profiles`, `record_query`, `record_get` |
| **servicenow-xml-docs** | Product documentation |
| **servicenow-xml-ui-examples** | UI Builder / Next Experience examples |

## Discovery workflow

1. Call Registry MCP (`search_records`, `lookup_by_name`, `lookup_script_include`, `get_workspace_app`).
2. Open the matching XML under **`update/`**.
3. Use **servicenow-xml-instance** when the question is live data rather than the export.
4. Do not broad-search **`author_elective_update/`** unless the task is deletes or residual app config.
